Package: pkghaus-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: OpenPGP archive keyring for apt.pkg.haus
 The keys apt uses to verify the pkg.haus APT archive. Installing this
 package keeps the trust anchor current: key rotations ship as ordinary
 package updates, signed by a key the system already trusts, so apt
 keeps working across a rotation with no manual step.
 .
 Two keyrings are installed. pkghaus-archive-keyring.gpg is the trust
 anchor an apt Signed-By line names, and carries only the key that signs
 the release files. pkghaus-source-keyring.gpg carries the key that signs
 source packages, kept separate because apt accepts any signing key in the
 keyring it is pointed at.
